I just got my second ascension yesterday (Barbarian, first was
Samurai), so I'm about in the same boat as you.

Lately, I've been trying to play pacifist gnomish healers, and as a
result, have done the protection racket successfully a half a dozen
times or so. It seems to almost be a 50/50 shot if I can do the racket,
which from what I hear isn't bad odds.

All that to say, playing pacifist healers has really expanded my
playing style a lot, though from personal experience, when you
bump-kill a jackal after you've finally got dragon scale armor and have
a nice pet dragon and 14 points of deity protection, it's *really*
annoying. So don't play too many of 'em (or else you'll drain your
vodka supply), but it's been a helpful (and complete) paradigm shift
from the combat-wombat that I'm used to.



